A token whose kind is read from data takes its theme color on fyne,
bubbletea and android.

fyne's span is built with its kind, and the build wrote `WithToken` only for a
kind it could read off a literal. A kind read from data -- each run of an
`md.document` code sample, or a loop over runs as here -- was built with none,
and the palette's `SetColor` beside it says nothing while no palette is set,
so the run took no token's color. The kind is the constructor's expression now,
`WithToken(r.Kind)`, which the theme answers as it answers a literal one.

bubbletea and android looked the kind's color up while generating, so a kind
read from data had none to look up: the run fell back to the terminal's
foreground and to `Color.Unspecified`. Each now asks at run time what it would
have answered for a literal -- `tui.TokenColor` with the comment's faint
beside it, and a `when` over the kind giving its Material role -- as the
fallback the palette's color takes where it is unset.

-- main.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import markup "sngl:ui/markup"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

struct Run {
    kind markup.Token
    text string
}

ui.window #home(title="t") {
    markup.richText {
        for var r = [Run{kind=markup.Token.keyword, text="func"}, Run{kind=markup.Token.function, text="main"}] {
            markup.token(kind=r.kind) {
                markup.text(r.text)
            }
        }
    }
}
